# Backlog Track

Next.js 16 app for tracking university lecture backlogs and exam prep. Uses Firebase Auth, Supabase (Postgres) for data, Tailwind v4, and Framer Motion.

## Architecture

- **Frontend**: Single-page app in `src/components/AppShell.tsx` with two tabs: lectures and exams.
- **State hooks**: `src/hooks/useAppState.ts` (lectures/subjects) and `src/hooks/useExamState.ts` (exams/topics/practice tests). Both use optimistic updates with rollback on error.
- **API routes**: Next.js route handlers in `src/app/api/`. All require Bearer token auth via `verifyToken()`. DB columns use `snake_case`; client types in `src/lib/types.ts` use `camelCase`.
- **Styling**: CSS variables for theming (light/dark). Inline `style={}` with `var(--surface)`, `var(--fg)`, `var(--muted-fg)`, `var(--border-color)`, `var(--input-bg)`, etc. No CSS modules.

## Conventions

- Client IDs are generated with `uuid` v4 before API calls (optimistic insert pattern).
- Week-based lecture titles use helpers from `src/lib/weeks.ts` (`formatWeekTitle`, `parseWeekNumber`).
- Icons come from `lucide-react` only.
- All components are `"use client"` since the app is fully client-rendered inside `AuthGuard`.
